<title>USA: USDA offers $70 Mln export credits to Sri Lanka.</title>
<headline>USDA offers $70 Mln export credits to Sri Lanka.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said Friday it offered $70 million in short-term export credit guarantees to assist sales of wheat, wheat flour and semolina to Sri Lanka.</p>
<p>The GSM-102 credits would be available first-come, first-served for sales made during fiscal 1997, which ends Sept 30.</p>
<p>Coverage was offered on a free alongside or freight on board basis on up to 98 percent of the principal for 90 days to three years.</p>
</text>
